# .claude/worktree-deps — dev-platform's worktree-mode marker.
#
# Its presence is what puts this repo in worktree mode: /plan and /code give
# each session its own copy of the repo under .claude/worktrees/<branch>, so two
# concurrent sessions can never share a working tree or switch each other's
# branch. /merge tears the worktree down after the PR lands.
#
# The list below is deliberately EMPTY. A manifest names the heavy git-ignored
# runtime paths that must be symlinked into a fresh worktree for the app to run
# — and dev-platform has none: it ships rules, commands, skills and scripts, not
# a service. There is no .env, no node_modules, no build cache.
#
# link-deps.sh treats a manifest with no live paths as a clean no-op, so this
# file being comment-only is correct rather than unfinished. If dev-platform
# ever grows a runtime dependency, list one git-ignored path per line here;
# blank lines and # comments are ignored.
